        "reference": "Ether 9:23",
        "book": "Ether",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 23
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that his wife died, being an hundred and two years old. And it came to pass that Coriantum took to wife, in his old age, a young maid, and begat sons and daughters; wherefore he lived until he was an hundred and forty and two years old.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 24,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ether 9:24",
        "book": "Ether",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 24
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that he begat Com, and Com reigned in his stead; and he reigned forty and nine years, and he begat Heth; and he also begat other sons and daughters.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 25,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ether 9:25",
        "book": "Ether",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 25
      },
